Description: This package contains data and functions to allow users to explore
    and map ZCTA-level tornado exposures in the United States from 1996 onward.
    Data comes from the NOAA Storm Prediction Center Severe Weather Database, the
    National Weather Service Damage Assessment Toolkit and the Census Bureau.
    The complete SPC records and tracks are included, with the SPC values as
    given. Exposure can be defined by overlap, by the modeled share of the ZCTA's
    area or residents inside the path, or by the distance from the SPC line to
    the ZCTA's population-weighted centroid or boundary. The National Weather
    Service damage points, lines and polygons are included unmodified and are
    linked to the SPC tornadoes.
